 host.innerHTML=`<article class="ms-page"><section class="panel pad"><div class="kicker">AMBIENT FIELD · STOCHASTIC PARTICLES · DECLARED INTENT</div><h2>Intent within the field</h2><p>Particles represent an ambient field; prayer supplies a reference pattern within it. This is an interactive representation of your spiritual framework. The binary grid is the exact integer simulation snapshot, not a measurement of an external field.</p><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,360px),1fr));gap:16px;align-items:start"><div><canvas id="pfCanvas" width="1000" height="440" style="width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:16px" role="img" aria-label="Stochastic ambient-field particles with prayer-referenced intent and boundary hold/flip review"></canvas></div><div><h3>Pre-filter ASCII field</h3><p>Proposed motion bytes · ASCII 0–127; control codes are pictured.</p><pre id="pfAsciiPre" style="font-family:monospace;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;font-size:10px;line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:1px;padding:10px;background:#162b3a;color:#daeaf3;border-radius:16px"></pre><h3>Post-filter ASCII field</h3><p>Same tick and incoming positions · filtered direction bytes.</p><pre id="pfAsciiPost" style="font-family:monospace;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;font-size:10px;line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:1px;padding:10px;background:#162b3a;color:#daeaf3;border-radius:16px"></pre><p id="pfDifference"></p></div></div><div class="actions"><button id="pfMotion">${moving?'Pause':'Resume'} particles</button><button id="pfStep">Single step</button><label>Global branch<select id="pfBranch"><option>PASS</option><option>FAIL</option></select></label><label>Review policy<select id="pfPolicy"><option value="bounds">Keep proposed horizontal motion inside the field</option><option value="unknown">Unresolved · hold for review</option></select></label></div><p id="pfStats" role="status"></p><p><b>Exact flow:</b> seeded stochastic bit XOR Unified Flux orbit contribution XOR prayer-reference bit → proposed direction → explicit boundary review → good holds / evil flips / unknown holds → integer motion. PASS and FAIL have identical per-bit rules in your supplied logic. Independent boundary reflection remains a separate physical simulation rule.</p><p>The labels “good” and “evil” here classify only this declared movement criterion. They do not determine a person’s morality. Your prayer, four-way lessons and shared assessment engines provide broader reflection after a snapshot is submitted.</p></section><section class="panel pad"><h2>Exact binary flux grid</h2><p>48 particles · 20-byte header + 9 bytes per particle = 452 bytes / 3,616 bits. Coordinates and velocities use little-endian integer fields. The final byte stores raw, prayer, proposed and output bits, plus the review label.</p><label class="field">Inspect particle<input id="pfIndex" type="number" min="0" max="47" value="0"></label><pre id="pfParticle" style="white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere"></pre><details><summary>All exact snapshot bits · header and particles</summary><pre id="pfBits" style="white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;max-height:320px;overflow:auto"></pre></details><p id="pfExact"></p><details><summary>Exact pre-filter, post-filter and XOR bits</summary><pre id="pfStageBits" style="white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;max-height:320px;overflow:auto"></pre></details><button id="pfExport">Download exact snapshot</button></section><section class="panel pad"><h2>Feed shared neural processing</h2><p>Whole snapshot bits enter checked binary / ternary / qutrit transport, the classifier and recurrent field, plus discipline, Gnostic study, welfare, four-way and inference engines. These stages use the app’s available context; they are not an all-knowing moral oracle. Check the resulting job receipt to see what ran.</p><button id="pfSend">Process current snapshot</button><label class="toggle"><input id="pfAuto" type="checkbox" checked> Process one snapshot per minute while this page is visible</label><p id="pfStatus" role="status">Waiting for prayer reference.</p><details><summary>Shared processing receipts</summary><pre id="pfReceipts" style="white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere"></pre></details></section><section class="panel pad"><h2>Prayer and supplied source pattern</h2><p>The exact reference text is encoded in UTF-8. Its bits participate in the XOR input; the explicit review rule controls the hold/flip stage. Command-like phrases remain source text, not executable commands.</p><details><summary>Read the prayer, grid and source text</summary><pre id="pfPrayer" style="white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere"></pre></details><p id="pfReference"></p><details><summary>Canonical executable hold/flip rule</summary><pre>output = label === "evil" ? proposed ^ 1 : proposed;
// good and unknown hold; PASS and FAIL use the same mapping.
// No permission changes or external system commands.</pre></details></section></article>`;
